# The update-and-rollback states: from a newer signed release on the release host
# to Squire installed on it, rolled back from it, or left as it was.
# The record (journey.json) is minted from this file by rcf discover journey add.
# Every word of these states reaches the owner in Squire's own session, at
# claude.ai/code or in the Claude app; no window is added. The line grammar draws
# one line of steps per entry, so each branch from the main line is drawn as its
# own entry and exit: a refused release, the owner's no or no answer, a failed
# check and its rollback, a rollback whose own check fails, and an install that
# did not finish. The interruptions answer to the update criteria: a download
# that fails or is cut short, the owner leaving the chat or the request timing
# out, a restart part way through the install, and the owner on the phone.

# Journey: update-and-rollback
actor: A Squire owner whose Squire is running on their own Mac
goal: From a newer signed release to Squire running on it, or on the previous version, with the owner's folder unchanged
- entry weekly-check @claude-code-web The scheduler's weekly check reads latest.json from the release host; a newer release is downloaded into staging, outside core
- step verified @claude-code-web The check: the signature against the installed key, the manifest's known fields, every listed file with its digest and no unlisted file; the release is staged
- step offered @claude-code-web One wake-up tells the session; the session asks for the install and the safety floor's block carries the version and the changelog exactly as signed, which the session shows the owner as written
- step owner-yes @claude-code-web The owner says yes to that request; the yes names that version and is fresh
- step installing @claude-code-web The scheduler's next run installs from the installed release's own code: the install record written first, the new release kept, the runner stopped, core laid down, the agents reloaded
- step checking @claude-code-web The check: the runner and one live session back, every floor file at its digest, signed in, every core file against the signed manifest, and no process of the previous release left
- exit installed @claude-code-web Installed: one wake-up tells the owner Squire is updated; the release before the previous one is removed
- entry refused @claude-code-web A release the check refuses (unsigned, another key, altered, a file missing or unlisted, a field or answer it cannot read): its staging is removed and nothing of core, the kept releases, the agents or the owner's folder changes
- exit refused-named @claude-code-web The refusal is one health line until the next weekly check
- entry not-now @claude-code-web The owner says no, or does not answer before the request times out: core's digests and the kept releases stay as they are
- exit mentioned-again @claude-code-web The staged release is mentioned again at most once a week
- entry check-failed @claude-code-web The check after the install fails, or a line of it cannot be read
- step rolling-back @claude-code-web The install job, still the previous release's code, lays the previous release down again, switches back and reloads, with no one acting
- step checking-again @claude-code-web The check runs again on the previous release
- exit rolled-back @claude-code-web One wake-up names both versions: Squire rolled the update back
- entry rollback-check-failed @claude-code-web The check after the rollback fails too
- exit ticket-offered @claude-code-web A health line names both versions and a support ticket is offered
- entry interrupted @claude-code-web The install stopped part way: a restart, a power cut, a killed process or a log-out; its install record is still there
- step recovered @claude-code-web At the next runner start or scheduler tick: Squire stays on the new release when its files, the installed core's digests and the manifest all match and the check passes, otherwise it lays the previous release down
- exit told-which @claude-code-web One wake-up says which version Squire is on; the owner's folder is unchanged
interruptions: lostSignal=weekly-check, closedTab=offered, expiredLink=not-now, deadBattery=interrupted, switchedDevice=offered, lostEmail=notApplicable:Squire sends no email and no emailed link for an update; every word reaches the owner in Squire's own session
